# claudish sidecar — per-machine .env
#
# Copy to `.env` next to docker-compose.yml on a SIDECAR machine, then:
#   docker compose up -d --build
#
# The hub (po-2025) needs NONE of this: every value below defaults to the hub's
# current setup, so `docker compose up -d` with no .env keeps the hub unchanged.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in .env — CLAUDISH_PROXY_KEY is a secret.

# --- Host wiring -------------------------------------------------------------

# Profile dir holding config.json (API keys, routing, profiles). Mounted read-only.
CLAUDISH_CONFIG_DIR=C:\Users\<user>\.claudish

# Host port to publish. 3000 is taken on some machines (ai-01) — pick a free one.
CLAUDISH_HOST_PORT=3001

# Container name — only needs changing if you run more than one on a host.
CLAUDISH_CONTAINER_NAME=claudish-sidecar

# Canonical fleet id for THIS machine, e.g. myia-po-2024 (#345). install-sidecar.ps1
# -Machine writes it for you; it is listed here because a name absent from
# docker-compose.yml's environment: list never reaches the container (#304).
# It rides on the relay's OWN liveness probe so the hub attributes that probe to
# this machine instead of filing it as a header-less phantom lane. Leave empty on
# the hub — it has no relay branch, so it never sends that probe.
CLAUDISH_MACHINE=

# Capture dir (host side). Keep capture ON: in NOMINAL mode the relay path writes
# nothing (the hub captures centrally), so any file that DOES appear here is by
# construction an AUTONOMOUS-mode outage capture — the trail that
# reconcile-outage-captures.ps1 packs and merges back into the hub's archives.
# Sidecars have no nightly compaction job, so run that reconciliation after an
# outage rather than blinding yourself pre-emptively.
CLAUDISH_CAPTURE_HOST_DIR=.\captures
# Leave UNSET to capture. Set it empty (CLAUDISH_CAPTURE_DIR=) only on a
# disk-starved host — that silently destroys the outage-reconciliation trail.
#CLAUDISH_CAPTURE_DIR=

# --- Relay -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Shared cluster key. Same value as the `x-proxy-key` header in the machine's
# ~/.claude/settings.json (ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS). Read it, never print it.
CLAUDISH_PROXY_KEY=

# KEY ROTATION ONLY — the retiring key, kept accepted for a transition window.
# To rotate: put the NEW key in CLAUDISH_PROXY_KEY and the OLD one here, redeploy,
# repoint clients one by one (both keys work), then unset this and redeploy.
# Unset = single-key mode (normal operation).
#CLAUDISH_PROXY_KEY_PREVIOUS=

# Hub URL. Unset => this container IS the hub. Set => sidecar. The hub is po-2025
# at .50 since the 2026-09 migration — po-2023 (.46) is a RELAY now, never an
# upstream (relaying to it recreates the double-hop drift measured on po-2024/po-2026).
#   LAN (po-2024, po-2026, ai-01) : http://192.168.0.50:3000
#   WAN (a machine whose CONTAINER cannot reach .50 — diagnose from inside
#        the container first, see the runbook)  : https://models.myia.io
# Never set on the hub machine (po-2025): that recreates the 2026-09-19
# self-relay incident.
CLAUDISH_RELAY_UPSTREAM=http://192.168.0.50:3000

# 1 on a WAN upstream only. Leave empty on LAN.
CLAUDISH_RELAY_COMPRESS=

# Forward header budget in ms (#320). Empty = 360000 (the hub's own ~6-min
# header-phase contract: first-event watchdog 300s, transport retry 60s +
# patient backoff ~305s). Legal range 5000..600000; anything else (including 0
# and garbage) falls back to the default — an unbounded header wait is the
# never-hang violation the bound exists to prevent, so there is no "off".
# Lower it ONLY with measured hub header latency in hand: 30s was measured
# amputating legitimate GLM bursts (35-92s salves, queue to 221s).
CLAUDISH_RELAY_HEADER_TIMEOUT_MS=

# Leak-policy backstop: 1 on EVERY machine except ai-01, which is the only one
# authorized for native Anthropic models.
CLAUDISH_NO_ANTHROPIC=1

# --- Budget failover ---------------------------------------------------------
#
# Substitutes a whole ROLE (opus/sonnet/haiku/fable) when its metered plan runs dry,
# and says so in the next condensation. Different from FallbackHandler, which
# swaps providers for the same model.
#
# Set these on the machine that actually CALLS the models. A NOMINAL sidecar only
# relays, so on a sidecar they matter solely for AUTONOMOUS (hub-down) mode — the
# hub is where they normally belong.
#
# All empty => inert. Configuring a target does NOT activate it.

# Where each role goes when its budget is gone. Any routing spec getHandlerForRequest
# accepts (provider@model, custom endpoint name, bare model).
#
# A step that is OUR OWN capacity declares it inline with a `!own` suffix, e.g.
#   CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_HAIKU=vllm-myia@swift-1.5-27b:8!own>role:sonnet
# Such a step has no credit to exhaust: its non-quota failures (e.g. a 502 while the
# engine restarts) bench it on a SHORT capped ladder (30s -> 2m -> 5m) instead of the
# quota-sized one (10m -> ...), so a saturated local engine does not divert a whole
# role onto paid steps for 10 minutes at a time (#553 defect 2). A QUOTA-shaped
# refusal keeps the default ladder. The suffix is stripped before routing, so
# `:8` still means concurrency 8; an unknown class (!fast) warns and is ignored.
# Kill switch: CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_OWN_BACKOFF=0 reverts every `!own` to default.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_OPUS=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_OPUS_LABEL=
# degraded (default) | improved | lateral — how capability moves, from the
# agent's point of view. Unset means "degraded": never flatter the substitute.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_OPUS_DIRECTION=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_OPUS_NOTE=
# ISO 8601 wall-lift time per step. Empty entries preserve position. While in the
# FUTURE a declared date CLOSES the step outright (#261): never selected by the
# walk, never the last-step fallback — including a step that never failed (the
# 2026-09-25 closure on a healthy Qwen step served 865 responses; the recreate's
# state wipe is exactly when the closure starts biting). Once it passes the step
# is probeable again. A step that HAS failed keeps its own record's date — a
# body-parsed one wins over this config value.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_OPUS_RESET=

CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_SONNET=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_SONNET_LABEL=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_SONNET_DIRECTION=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_SONNET_NOTE=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_SONNET_RESET=

CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_HAIKU=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_HAIKU_LABEL=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_HAIKU_DIRECTION=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_HAIKU_NOTE=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_HAIKU_RESET=

# Leave this block empty while modelMap.fable maps Fable directly to Astra.
# A nominal target must never also be a failover step: that would retry the
# same walled target and emit a misleading fallback notice. When native Fable
# becomes nominal again, set Astra here atomically with removing that mapping.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_FABLE=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_FABLE_LABEL=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_FABLE_DIRECTION=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_FABLE_NOTE=
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_FABLE_RESET=

# Force a role onto its substitute NOW, no upstream error needed. Comma-separated
# (e.g. `opus,haiku`), or `none`. Use to conserve a plan before it is exhausted.
# `role@machine` (e.g. `haiku@myia-po-2027`) diverts that role for ONE machine's
# requests only (matched on X-Claudish-Machine); the other machines stay nominal.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_ACTIVE=

# Per-machine step exclusion (#693): "stepTarget:machine1 machine2" — comma
# separates entries, machines within one entry are space-separated, and the
# split is at the LAST colon so a `role:sonnet` target stays whole. The cascade
# stays ONE global list per role; a machine named here skips the listed steps
# in every walk (armed, walled, overload) with no mark and no wall — the step
# simply does not exist for that machine. Case-insensitive on both sides.
# Typical use: `vllm-myia@swift-1.5-27b:myia-ai-01` keeps a machine whose
# prompts are structurally too large for the local engine OFF it when the
# nominal walls, while every other machine keeps it as step 0.
# ⚠ Startup read (initFailover) — a flip needs a recreate.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_STEP_EXCLUDE=

# Model-name → role aliases (pattern:role, comma-separated, lowercase substring
# match) for clients that request the nominal model by NAME (e.g. `glm-5.3`,
# `MiniMax-M3`) instead of a role keyword (`claude-sonnet-4-6`). Role keywords
# win when both match; unset = keywords only. Remove once all agents send role names.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_ROLE_MODELS=

# 1 = also switch automatically when upstream reports genuine quota/credit
# exhaustion. A plain per-minute 429 does NOT trigger it — only a real plan wall.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_AUTO=

# Grace before arming (#91): consecutive qualifying nominal refusals required
# before the role exiles to its cascade. 1 restores the arm-on-first-refusal
# behaviour. A nominal success clears the run. A 429 naming a short retry-after
# never counts at all — that is a burst, not a wall.
# ⚠ Container deployments (#304): these five knobs reach the process ONLY
# through docker-compose.yml's environment: list (they are in it since #304).
# The env file alone interpolates nothing the compose list does not name, and
# these are STARTUP reads (initFailover) — a flip takes effect at the next
# recreate, unlike the *_THINKING knobs below which are re-read per request.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_ARM_AFTER=2
# When > 0, an under-threshold refusal waits this long (ms) and retries the
# NOMINAL once inside the same request before surfacing the 429. 0 = off.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_ARM_GRACE_MS=0
# Bursts below this retry-after (ms, header or body-named delay) never arm.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_ARM_RETRY_AFTER_CEILING_MS=120000
# Per-session dwell (#91): minimum time (ms) a session keeps its resolved
# cascade step, so an in-flight conversation cannot flip providers mid-work
# (each flip re-colds the prompt cache at both ends). Sliding: an active
# session renews it; an idle one's pin lapses. 0 = off.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_SESSION_DWELL_MS=600000
# Nominal-recovery yield: how long (ms) a VERIFIED nominal recovery (a real
# request served by the nominal, not a wall-TTL expiry that only starts a
# probe) must hold before dwell pins yield back to the nominal. Bounds an
# intermittent wall's isolated success to one switch per arm cycle. A re-arm
# voids the marker. 0 = yield as soon as the recovery is verified.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_RECOVERY_GRACE_MS=120000
# #299-B one-shot overload walk. When a request's NOMINAL fails with a
# transient provider overload (HTTP 529, a 429/503 the patient backoff
# exhausted into a 529, or a 400 connection_error), the cascade tries its
# FIRST SERVABLE step ONCE for that request only — skipping steps in backoff,
# walled buckets, or closed by a future _RESET (#261 closure) — and writes no
# FAILURE state (no arm, no stepFailed mark, no bucket wall, no dwell pin; a
# served attempt still resets the step's failure count, which a wall never
# feeds): the moment the overload lifts, the
# next request re-probes the nominal instead of riding a cascade the role was
# never exiled to. The native (Anthropic) lane never walks: its meter is the
# client's own credential. A step that also fails surfaces the ORIGINAL
# overload, never the step's own incident. Read per request (flip without a
# recreate); only "0" disarms.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_OVERLOAD_WALK=

# #348 — walk time budget (ms), measured from the request entering the
# cascade (transport ladder + patient backoff + nominal latency all count
# against it). A 429/503 overload reaches the walk at ~365 s already — past
# the relay's 360 s header deadline (its output unread: the sidecar fell
# through and served locally) and cramping the 600 s client timeout for a
# direct client whose walk step is also slow. Default 300000 keeps the direct
# sum under 600 s while fast direct 529s (the measured driver, seconds) still
# walk; 0 = no bound. (No client-gone skip exists: an abort is undetectable
# pre-write on this stack — budget-failover.md §One-shot overload walk.)
# Read per request.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_WALK_BUDGET_MS=

# #431 — step-skip kill switch. A cascade step that cannot take the request
# (context overflow answered as a recovery turn, or a saturated endpoint
# limiter) normally skips FORWARD to the next step — no failure mark, no dwell
# pin on the skipped step. "0" restores the pre-#431 behavior: the recovery
# turn / the unbounded limiter wait becomes the client's answer. Read per
# request.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_STEP_SKIP=

# #431 — bounded busy wait for a CASCADE STEP attempt (ms): when the endpoint
# limiter (customEndpoints maxConcurrency) stays full past this, the request
# skips to the next step. Default 2000; 0 = off (unbounded FIFO, today's
# behavior). The NOMINAL path never reads it — an unconfigured or direct
# endpoint keeps its unbounded wait whatever this says. Read per request.
CLAUDISH_FAILOVER_STEP_BUSY_WAIT_MS=

# #317 option B — per-session output-token ceiling. Counts UPSTREAM output
# tokens (every cascade attempt the request pays) per (X-Claudish-Machine,
# session_id) over a 24 h sliding window; subagents share the parent's
# session_id, so a swarm feeds ONE counter (measured 2026-10-12, session
# bc377615: 5 parent turns + 230 subagent reqs, same sid). Both knobs in
# output tokens; empty = that bar is inert (no counting, no refusal).
#   CEILING — refusal bar: at the bar the request is answered locally with a
#             labeled 429 + retry-after = the real remaining window, BEFORE
#             any upstream is paid. The body wording is deliberately free of
#             quota-class words — isQuotaExhaustion must never arm the budget
#             failover off our own ceiling (pinned against the real predicate).
#   WARN    — WARN-only bar: a [SessionBudgetCeiling] WARN marker fires once
#             per crossing (forceConsole). With only CEILING armed, WARN
#             defaults to 80% of it. The fleet-wide pose is WARN-only until
#             the user fixes the values. Read per request — but in a container
#             a NEW value still enters only at the next recreate (#310).
CLAUDISH_SESSION_BUDGET_CEILING=
CLAUDISH_SESSION_BUDGET_WARN=

# Qwen reasons by default and the Token Plan bills on OUTPUT tokens.
# disabled (default) | passthrough | budget:<n>. Read per request — flip it
# during a crunch without restarting the proxy everyone depends on.
CLAUDISH_QWEN_THINKING=

# GLM reasons by default; the switch is binary (no budget control, unlike Qwen).
# passthrough (default) | disabled. Read per request.
CLAUDISH_GLM_THINKING=

# DeepSeek reasons by default and PAYG bills on OUTPUT tokens. Measured
# 2026-09-01 on deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp: disabling took a realistic
# tool-calling turn from 213 to 92 output tokens with an identical tool call.
# passthrough (default, historical behavior) | disabled. Read per request.
CLAUDISH_DEEPSEEK_THINKING=

# M3 does not reason unless asked (absent/disabled -> no thinking); M3.1-Flash
# differs: it thinks with the field omitted, and `disabled` is a 400/2013.
# passthrough (default) | disabled | forced[:<n>] (default n=16000) |
# effort:<low|medium|high|xhigh|max>. Read per request.
# `effort:<level>` (M3.1-Flash only) injects output_config.effort — the
# DOCUMENTED thinking-depth slider; Flash defaults to MAX when the field is
# absent, the dominant output-token driver on the Flash lane (2026-10-19:
# median thinking 1.5k chars, 23 responses >5k tokens). budget_tokens is not
# in the Anthropic-compat doc; whether Flash honors it is unmeasured (forced
# never rewrites a client-requested budget, and production clients send
# 31999) — effort is the first lever that reaches those requests. Applies
# regardless of the client's own thinking request; ignored with a log for
# non-Flash models.
# Shares `forced`'s filter semantics (#295/#324 chain) since Flash always
# thinks. `forced` rewrites an absent/disabled request to enabled — the model
# then reasons, and since #295 the thinking blocks (with their signature) PASS
# THROUGH to the client: M3 only restarts thinking on a tool-continuation turn
# when the preceding assistant turn carries its preserved thinking block, so a
# client that never receives the blocks can never echo them and the chain mutes
# (the 1/30 production shape). An enabled OR adaptive client keeps its own
# setting. The unrequested-thinking strip still applies under passthrough.
# Since #324 B1 the RETURN trip is covered too: under `forced` the history
# strip keeps MiniMax's OWN thinking blocks (unsigned or 64-hex digest
# signature — M3's implicit signature is the SHA-256 of the empty string)
# while foreign ones (an Anthropic blob signature from an Opus session that
# fell to a MiniMax cascade step) stay stripped. Unforced policies strip
# everything, exactly as before.
# NOTE: on the hub corpus (2026-09-23) ~77% of haiku-lane requests already
# send enabled/31999 and still almost never reason — `forced` does not
# change those; it only rewrites the absent/disabled one-shots. Verify an
# armed `forced` from output_tokens or the resp-* captures (taken AFTER the
# filter — under `forced` they should now show thinking blocks).
CLAUDISH_MINIMAX_THINKING=

# --- Web search ---------------------------------------------------------------
#
# SearXNG endpoint used by the WebSearch interception. The committed compose
# default is the public URL, which sits behind IIS Basic Auth since 2026-08-19:
# credentials go in the URL userinfo (standard curl form) and are never logged.
#   LAN machines : http://192.168.0.47:8181          (no auth, bypasses IIS)
#   WAN machines : https://<user>:<pass>@search.myia.io
# Get the account from the operator (Windows account on the IIS host) — never
# commit a filled-in value.
SEARXNG_URL=http://192.168.0.47:8181

# --- Durable context state (#651) ---------------------------------------------
#
# Learned context caps (`short-circuit … (learned)`) used to live in memory only:
# every recreate forgot them, and the band between the engine's real window and
# the reported floor stayed open until a refusal re-taught it. The committed
# compose default points at the writable model-cache volume, so nothing needs
# setting here. An EXPLICIT empty disables persistence (memory-only, the
# pre-#651 behaviour).
#   CLAUDISH_OVERFLOW_CAPS_PATH=/var/cache/claudish/overflow-caps.json
CLAUDISH_OVERFLOW_CAPS_PATH=
# #660 r1 — a restored cap is bounded by its own `at` stamp, so persistence
# cannot turn a mis-taught cap into a permanent refusal. Default 24 h in the
# code (the effective pre-#651 lifetime: the nightly watchdog restart); `0` =
# no expiry. Empty = the default (empty does NOT mean "off" here).
#   CLAUDISH_OVERFLOW_CAPS_MAX_AGE_MS=86400000
CLAUDISH_OVERFLOW_CAPS_MAX_AGE_MS=
# --- #654: in-flight token budget per endpoint --------------------------------
#
# A local engine saturates on CONTEXT, not request count (measured 2026-10-24:
# six ~200K-token bodies = 1.2M KV tokens against 750,747 available -> ~1
# token/s for 20 min, 58 preemptions, watchdog restart). Two knobs bound what
# an endpoint admits, evaluated BEFORE the upstream call on the #431 busy wire:
# an over-budget step is never called and the cascade advances with NO failure
# mark; on the nominal it is an overload-class diversion (one-shot walk).
#
#   CLAUDISH_ENDPOINT_TOKEN_BUDGET_<NAME>  sum of in-flight ESTIMATED tokens
#   CLAUDISH_ENDPOINT_BIG_LIMIT_<NAME>     max CONCURRENT requests over 100K
#
# <NAME> is the custom-endpoint name uppercased, non-alphanumerics as "_"
# (vllm-myia -> VLLM_MYIA). Estimate = serialized body bytes / 3.5 (measured
# 914,723 B / 262,145 real tokens = 3.49). A resubmission of an identical
# body (same machine+session) REPLACES its predecessor's estimate instead of
# adding a second one, so a client echo never trips the budget on itself.
# Unset = inert (AC1); garbage or "0" = inert (a typo must not invent a
# budget). Measured anchor: engine KV 750,747 -> try SUM ~550000, BIG_LIMIT 3.
#
# NOTE (compose deployments): the environment: list in docker-compose.yml is
# an explicit allowlist (#310) and these names are per-endpoint, so the repo
# lists the literal for the endpoint this deployment arms (VLLM_MYIA —
# already in compose) and every OTHER endpoint adds its own line there, e.g.
#   - CLAUDISH_ENDPOINT_TOKEN_BUDGET_QWEN_PLAN=${CLAUDISH_ENDPOINT_TOKEN_BUDGET_QWEN_PLAN:-}
# then set the value here and recreate (-Recreate -EnvFile).
#
# NOTE (per-process registry): the budget counts in-flight tokens PER PROCESS.
# A sidecar in AUTONOMOUS mode keeps its own registry — the hub and a
# sidecar calling the same engine each admit up to the full SUM independently,
# so the Σ of every process's budget must fit the engine's KV (750,747).
# With two callers, budget each at most ~half; the engine is the shared wall.
#
# Inert below — uncomment and name YOUR endpoint to arm.
# CLAUDISH_ENDPOINT_TOKEN_BUDGET_VLLM_MYIA=
# CLAUDISH_ENDPOINT_BIG_LIMIT_VLLM_MYIA=
